course: dictionary
lesson: 5741
title: Loudly
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Loudly is an adverb. It tells us how something is done, and it answers the question how? When you speak loudly, you use a strong voice so people can hear you far away. «The dog barked loudly» tells us how the dog barked: with a lot of noise.
explain: Use the words around loudly to check its meaning. In «yell loudly "No!"», the word yell already tells you about a big voice, so loudly means in a strong voice that carries. Then try your meaning in the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have it.
explain: Loudly is not the same as noisy. Noisy describes a place or a thing, like a noisy playground, while loudly describes how someone or something makes a sound. Useful phrases to learn: speak loudly, laugh loudly, shout loudly, loudly and clearly.
fact: Loudly means in a loud way, making a lot of noise or with a strong voice that can be heard far away.
fact: Loudly is an adverb, so it tells how something is done: «The shoebill clatters its beak loudly.»
fact: «Marmots whistle loudly when they see an eagle or a fox, warning the others to run to their burrows.»
fact: Speak loudly and clearly when you present in class, but do not shout loudly in the library or during quiet times.
fact: In an emergency, shout loudly «Help!» or «No!» so that people can hear you.
exercise: «The shoebill clatters its beak loudly.» What does loudly tell us about the clattering? | It was done very slowly | It was done in the morning | It was done by a very small bird | *It was done with a lot of noise
exercise: «Chloe's first drama club, a girl with a ponytail says loudly "Ugh, newbie" and rolls her eyes.» Which word tells you how the girl spoke? | *loudly | eyes | says | girl
exercise: Which is the best way to speak when you present to your class? | Mumble quietly at the floor | Whisper loudly into the microphone | *Speak loudly and clearly so everyone can hear | Shout loudly during quiet reading time
test: «Marmots whistle loudly when they see an eagle.» Why do they whistle loudly? | To show they are sleepy | To say goodnight to each other | To look for food | *To warn the others to run to their burrows
test: In «shout loudly "Help!"», what does loudly mean? | In a happy, singing way | Quietly and secretly | *In a strong voice that can be heard far away | Sadly and slowly
exam: Nadia says loudly and noisy mean the same thing. Who is right? | Nadia is right, because they are always the same word | Nadia is right, if the room is quiet | Nadia is wrong, because loudly means quietly | *Nadia is wrong, because loudly tells how a sound is made, while noisy describes a place or thing
